  "body": "[This is interesting part of spec describing how browsers's API should cooperate with browser's environment when user activation had been commited](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/interaction.html#tracking-user-activation). \r\nFor the readers I see following confusing things:\r\n- Absent examples of APIs that would give you understanding about that which of APIs relates to [one or another type of user activation](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/interaction.html#user-activation-gated-apis).\r\n- Absent notification in spec that performation the author code in dev-tools run [activation triggering input event](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/interaction.html#activation-triggering-input-event) (Chrome does, Firefox doesn't)\r\n  \r\n  >  - Run the next code (in Chrome browser): `setInterval(() => console.log(navigator.userActivation.isActive), 1000)`. Some time you will being see `true` value. \r\n  >  - When you will see `false` value - perform any other code in console of dev-tools (after that you will see again `true` value). \r\n  > <br>\r\n  >\r\n  > **Conclusion**: performation code in dev-tools also running [activation triggering input event](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/interaction.html#activation-triggering-input-event), but you cost to notice that I noticed it in Chrome browser, probably it's bug.\r\n\r\nI think spec should describe cases [in that place](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/interaction.html#user-activation-gated-apis). But for now this is abstraction without concreticism.",
